<BaseLayout title="Methodology | GearPilot AI" description="The transparent standing desk eligibility and scoring methodology used by GearPilot AI." canonicalPath="/methodology/">
  <h1>How we compare standing desks</h1>
  <p>First, we filter to the US market and require a verified product record, a fresh known total price, fresh in-stock availability, workspace dimensions, height range, lift capacity, and any required electric adjustment. Unknown fields never pass a hard requirement.</p>
  <p>Eligible products receive a deterministic comparison score. Value weights price most heavily; quality weights capacity and warranty; workspace fit weights desktop size and height range. The calculation uses documented price, dimensions, capacity, warranty, and evidence status—never affiliate commission rates.</p>
  <p>A verified record includes source provenance for the product and its documented specifications. Price observations expire after seven days and in-stock observations after three days; stale or unknown offers are excluded rather than guessed. A partially verified record is research-only. A demo record is clearly marked synthetic and can never be presented as a real listing, price, review, or hands-on test.</p>
  <p>Scores compare the eligible catalog entries for the selected criteria. They are not star ratings or claims of hands-on testing.</p>
</BaseLayout>
